  "body": "The single-file HTML demos run a whole organism in the browser but had no automated regression cover \u2014 CI only certified the Python substrate. This adds a **Playwright** smoke test + a GitHub Actions job (**Demo Smoke**) that, for each demo, asserts it mounts with no unexpected console errors, exposes its engine, and passes its in-browser checks:\n\n- **Reference Agent:** Genome present, `activeBodyRefs` is populated-slots-only, dangling vs. unsupported ref labeling correct, and the `B-GEN` self-audit row is present.\n- **Spreadsheet:** its Stage-1 self-audit (`mantleSelfAuditV23`) returns **PASS**.\n\nThe assertions mirror the manual preview-harness checks used to develop the recent fixes, so this locks them against regression. **Verified locally end-to-end against real chromium: `DEMO SMOKE PASSED`.**\n\nNode lives only under `examples/tests/` (gitignored `node_modules`); the Python project stays dependency-free. Also aligned the existing audit workflow's stale header (`v3` / `32 invariants` \u2192 `Gen-4` / `68`) and noted `tests/` in the README tree + `examples/README`.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
